// PLAT-51: A LIST PANE'S SCROLLBAR IS A SCRUBBER over the pane's whole
// population (Scrollbar-Scrubbers.md): the Event Log, the Call Trace and the
// Terminal Output's line view. The container's own scrollbar is hidden — its
// track would PAGE on a click — and `views/list_scrubber_dom.nim` draws the
// track over the container's right edge: a click JUMPS there, the thumb
// drags the view, a tick marks where the debugger is.

// Only the VERTICAL bar is the scrubber's: the horizontal one stays, so a
// list wider than its pane (the Call Trace's long argument lists) can still
// be scrolled sideways (Nikolay, 2026-10-16).  It was `scrollbar-width: none`
// + `display: none`, which removed both.  `scrollbar-width` must stay unset:
// once it is, Chromium ignores the `::-webkit-scrollbar` rules entirely.  The
// remaining bar takes the app-wide scrollbar look (shared_widgets.styl).
.ct-scrubbed
  &::-webkit-scrollbar
    width: 0

.ct-list-scrubber
  position: absolute
  right: 0
  // The app-wide scrollbar's thickness (PANEL_SCROLLBAR_SIZE, 8px —
  // shared_widgets.styl): a scrubber is the pane's scrollbar and reads as one.
  width: PANEL_SCROLLBAR_SIZE
  // Above the pane's own overlays (the event log's DataTables footer sits
  // over the bottom of its scroll body): the track takes the press there.
  z-index: 30
  // NO HAND. The track is the pane's scrollbar, and a scrollbar is drawn with
  // the default cursor, the way the app-wide (native) one is; the hand would
  // say the track is a control a click activates, which it is not
  // (Pointer-Affordances). Its press and drag are the scrollbar's.
  background: transparent

.ct-list-scrubber-thumb
  // Drawn exactly as the app-wide scrollbar thumb (shared_widgets.styl):
  // the track's full width, square, flush with the panel's right edge, and
  // the same tokens — `tertiary`, stepping LIGHTER to `tertiary-hover` under
  // the pointer and while dragged.
  position: absolute
  left: 0
  right: 0
  background: colors-ui-surface-primary-tertiary

  &:hover,
  .ct-list-scrubber:active &
    background: colors-ui-surface-primary-tertiary-hover

.ct-list-scrubber-mark
  position: absolute
  left: 0
  right: 0
  // The execution pointer's colour, as the terminal's and GPUI's marks.
  background: colors-editor-action-secondary

// PLAT-70 (Horizontal-Overflow.md §4.7): a text pane's overflow-only
// HORIZONTAL bar — the vertical track's drawing on the other axis, along the
// scroll container's bottom (`views/list_scrubber_dom.attachHorizontalScrubber`),
// only while the content is wider than the pane. The square where it meets
// the vertical track belongs to neither.
// The container's own horizontal bar is hidden (its vertical one is the list
// scrubber's to hide, `.ct-scrubbed`); `scrollbar-width` stays unset for the
// reason given above.
.ct-hscrubbed
  &::-webkit-scrollbar
    height: 0

.ct-hscrubber
  position: absolute
  // The app-wide scrollbar's thickness, as the vertical track's
  // (`list_scrubber_dom.TrackPx` lays the two out against each other).
  height: PANEL_SCROLLBAR_SIZE
  z-index: 30
  // NO HAND. The track is the pane's scrollbar, and a scrollbar is drawn with
  // the default cursor, the way the app-wide (native) one is; the hand would
  // say the track is a control a click activates, which it is not
  // (Pointer-Affordances). Its press and drag are the scrollbar's.
  background: transparent

.ct-hscrubber-thumb
  // Drawn as the vertical thumb is: the track's full height, square, the
  // app-wide scrollbar's tokens.
  position: absolute
  top: 0
  bottom: 0
  background: colors-ui-surface-primary-tertiary

  &:hover,
  .ct-hscrubber:active &
    background: colors-ui-surface-primary-tertiary-hover
